Klaus Kassner wrote:
> Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote (schrieb, a écrit):
>
>> A cursed unicorn horn will do in a pinch, *if* you also
>> have a blessed one, but the recommended method is a
>> forgotten low-level spell. 
>
> Why low-level? You do not use up power for spells that you cannot cast
> anymore. Confusion is free. So you can also cast a high-level spell that
> you forgot.

Timing and odds.  It takes a long time to forget a spell so it matters
how early in the game you learned it. On the average low level spells
are easier to read so there's a better chance you've forgotten a low
level than a high level spell.

If all you ever intend to use spells for is confusion it doesn't matter.
On the one hand any blessed spellbook as early in the game as possible
will do.  On the other hand blessing a spellbook early as possible
spends a holy water that is a valuable item that early in the game.

